: Calculates the prime factors of a natural number n.
: If there are more factors remaining, HLT will be displayed.
: No HLT is displayed if there are no more factors.
: Note that this algorithm takes a considerable amount of time, as there is
: no direct way to check weather a number is whole.
: Figuring out how this works is left as an exercise for the reader.

: -01-          n

01  ENT         : n
02  MIN
03  GOTO [7]
04. 1
05  =
06  X-M
07  HLT
08  -
09  GOTO [1]
10  GOTO [-6]
11. 1
12  =
13  X-M
14  STO
15   [1]
16. 1
17  M+
18  GOTO [1]
19  GOTO [-9]
20  RCL
21   [1]
22  /
23  MR
24  GOTO [2]
25  GOTO [-9]
26  GOTO [-7]
27  -
28  1
29. =
30  X>0 [-1]
31  +/-
32  X>0 [-7]
33  GOTO [1]
34  GOTO [-8]
35  RCL
36   [1]
37  /
38  MR
39  -
40  1
41  +
42  X>0 [-8]
43  C
44  X-M
